            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "From Skechers to Foot Locker: Tariff chaos spurs record-high footwear, apparel deals",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "-U.S. President Donald Trump's trade war is helping to push U.S. clothing\u00a0and footwear acquisitions to all-time highs this year, with some companies merging to help offset tariff costs while others go private to weather the next 3-1/2 years of his presidency outside of the public market, dealmakers say.  Popular sneaker company Skechers announced a $9.42 billion deal in early May to go private days after it pulled its annual earnings forecasts and sent a letter, along with 75 other footwear companies, telling Trump the tariffs were an \"existential threat\" to the industry.  Sneaker seller Foot Locker, which also signed the letter to Trump, in May accelerated its $2.4 billion sale to Dick's Sporting Goods.",
